let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Poll</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">Ready</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">as_mut</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"n\">poll</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"k\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cx</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>with <code>wasmtime</code> at bytecodealliance/wasmtime@ffbf0e0c13, prints:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cargo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span>\n<span class=\"n\">trap</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">is_valid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">true</span>\n<span class=\"n\">trap</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Ok</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I32</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n<span class=\"n\">component</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">is_valid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">true</span>\n<span class=\"n\">component</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Ok</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I32</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">340539887</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Both handles should be invalid, because their frames are gone by then. Instead, <code>local</code> reads stale stack memory. With a <code>funcref</code> local, the same stale read builds a <code>Func</code> from a guest-written pointer and segfaults. The same happens for handles taken in <code>DebugEvent::HostcallError</code> and <code>DebugEvent::Exception</code> handlers.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
